PTX TMA-load+complete-tx-not-transitive
"The complete-tx orders only the copy's own operations, not the issuing thread's earlier store to h (6897, D19): P1, waiting on the mbarrier, may read h stale. Here P0 arrives before the store, so its arrive does not order h either. Expected: allowed."
{
g=5;
h=0;
d=0 @cta 0;
b=mbarrier(1) @cta 0;
P1:r0=0;
P1:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0                                                  | P1@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0                       ;
 mbarrier.arrive.expect_tx.release.cta b, 1                                | mbarrier.test_wait.parity.acquire.cta r0, b, 0 ;
 st.weak.global h, 1                                                       | ld.weak.global r1, h                           ;
 cp.async.bulk.shared::cluster.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes d, g, b |                                                ;
exists
(P1:r0 == 1 /\ P1:r1 == 0)
